{
  // Type-check program for the build/tooling suite. vitest runs these files
  // through esbuild transpile-only, so without this gate every type-level
  // contract in test/build (the `@ts-expect-error` pins on the untyped .mjs
  // imports, the workflow/SBOM parsing helpers) is erased and never enforced.
  //
  // These tests exercise the BUILD side of the repo — esbuild configs, the
  // scripts/ tooling, the packaged workflow YAML — so the compiler view is
  // Node + ESM, with no DOM lib and no vscode-webview types.
  //
  // The scripts/ and esbuild.config.mjs modules they import are plain .mjs with
  // no bundled types. Every one of those imports carries a line-scoped
  // `@ts-expect-error` on the module specifier — it self-verifies (goes red the
  // day the module gains types) and leaves everything the test itself authors
  // checked. As of 2026-08-28 no file here uses a file-level `@ts-nocheck`,
  // which would switch the WHOLE file off and make any type-level assertion in
  // it vacuous; five suites sat in that state from the day this config landed
  // (2026-08-22) until the swap.
  //
  // ⚠️ When a wrapping binding list would push the specifier off the directive's
  // line, use a namespace import and destructure below — a wrapped named import
  // silently unsuppresses (theme-palettes.test.ts documents the measurement).
  //
  // The tripwire against drifting back is no-file-level-ts-nocheck.test.ts, and
  // it is the AUTHORITY — for this directory and for the rest of the repo. As
  // of 2026-08-30 it no longer walks a directory: `discoverProjects` enumerates
  // the repo's tsconfigs, treats the ones no other config `extends` as the
  // programs (a deliberate heuristic — the test says so, and pins a roster of
  // the result), builds each of those, and asks the program's own SourceFiles
  // whether tsc opted them out. That makes containment and byte decoding tsc's
  // answers rather than the guard's, which is what let two hand-rolled layers be
  // deleted instead of extended. Run
  // `pnpm vitest run test/build/no-file-level-ts-nocheck.test.ts`.
  //
  // Two gates hold it up, named here by function only: `findConfigFiles` walks
  // everything outside dot-directories and outside its `SKIP_DIRS`, keeping the
  // files whose NAME matches its tsconfig pattern, and the "covers every
  // project `pnpm compile` and `pnpm compile:webview` type-check" cross-check
  // reads those two scripts, so a config the walk missed but the compile gate
  // names goes red. What escapes both is a program the walk cannot see that no
  // compile script names — rooted in a dot-directory, or under a `SKIP_DIRS`
  // name, or called something the pattern does not match — and invoked
  // directly, say by a workflow step running `tsc -p .tooling/tsconfig.json`.
  //
  // ⛔ Do NOT restate the boundaries here. Where each sits, why the `SKIP_DIRS`
  // names do not share one authority, why relaxing the dot-directory skip is
  // not the answer, and which directive forms and encodings the oracle detects
  // are each stated once next to the code that enforces them — the `SKIP_DIRS`
  // comment and that file's fixtures. This header re-derived those mechanics in
  // its own English three review cycles running and shipped a wrong claim every
  // time; its job is WHY the guard is built this way and WHERE the authority
  // lives, not to be the authority.
  // ⚠️ Asking tsc is not over-engineering. Four hand-rolled approximations were
  // tried first and every one shipped a silent miss: a block-comment strip that
  // swallowed live directives, a trivia walk that stopped at a shebang, a
  // whitespace class narrower than tsc's, and a read layer that handed the
  // oracle a different string than tsc reads. Every miss pointed the same
  // dangerous way — file reported clean, checking actually off.
  //
  // There is no grep that substitutes for it. Measured in PR #382: POSIX
  // `[[:space:]]` coverage varies by grep build and locale, misses U+0085 and
  // U+200B, and grep can model neither comment trivia, nor a shebang, nor a
  // UTF-16 file. Run the test.
  //
  // noEmit (inherited): this is a CI gate, not a build step — vitest still runs
  // through its own transpiler. rootDir is pinned to the repo root explicitly
  // (matching the sibling test tsconfigs) so the program's containment boundary
  // is stated rather than inferred — the ../../src/shared files sit outside
  // test/build/, and an inferred rootDir would silently widen with the include.
  // It plays no part in resolving that cross-layer import: rootDir governs emit
  // layout and the TS6059 containment check only, never module resolution.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["es2022"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "rootDir": "../.."
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "../../src/shared/**/*.ts"]
}
